# 08 Table and column descriptions - 2026-11-17T18:05:16Z
Docs check: https://docs.databricks.com/api/uc-catalogs/v1/catalog covers only catalog-level comments; it says nothing about table/column comments or refresh behavior, so behavior was tested directly.

## Experiment results (pipeline gold_system_risk, a materialized view)
1. COMMENT ON TABLE ... 'TEST manual table comment' -> after a pipeline update the comment reverted to the pipeline's own comment=. Manual comments on pipeline-managed tables do NOT persist.
2. ALTER TABLE ... ALTER COLUMN on a materialized view -> error EXPECT_TABLE_NOT_VIEW (treated as a view).
3. Column metadata via Column.alias(metadata={'comment':...}) -> 0 comments written (approach abandoned).
4. schema= DDL with COMMENT in @dlt.table -> comments written, and still present after a second refresh. This is what lakeflow/pipeline.py uses.

